# THE TAG HALF'S END-OF-RUN HOLE: a qualified injection the core never consumed was reported MISSING.
# Found triaging a round-1 dry-run failure of gen_ut_lockstep_icache_ecc_tag_two at seed 508609593.
#
# THE DEFECT, and it was an asymmetry inside one checker. At the end of a run report_phase treated the two
# injection kinds differently: kind inject_data with a valid way became verdict -1 and was counted as pending and
# UNJUDGED, with the code's own comment reading "the run ended before their verdict: unjudged, reported, never
# failed"; kind inject was set to verdict = qualified and close_owed then raised alert_minor for it. So the data
# half had an end-of-run allowance and the tag half had NONE. The tag half's qualification tests only that the
# cache is enabled and no invalidation sweep is near; it never tested whether the lookup was CONSUMED.
#
# WHY THAT MATTERS: the DUT checks a lookup it consumes. A tag word read on a lookup the core never consumes can
# never produce alert_minor_o, and at the end of a run that is exactly what happens.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT THAT SETTLED IT, from the failing run reproduced locally with the export on so the retirement
# stream is visible. The injected index was resolved against every retired record, taking the index as the pc bits
# above the line offset with 256 lines from the rendered lines-times-ways constant:
#     the run's LAST retirement is at cycle 21478
#     the injection is at cycle 21479, ONE CYCLE AFTER IT
#     retirements at or after the injection: ZERO
#     positive control, so the index mapping is not the story: index 28 is retired 18 times in the run, the last at
#     cycle 21478 with pc 0x800000e4, which maps to index 28
# The corrupted word was read one cycle after the core retired its last instruction.
#
# THE RULE, mirroring the data half rather than approximating it: a qualified tag injection with no pulse and NO
# RECORD RETIRED AT OR AFTER its cycle is UNJUDGED, counted as unconsumed and never failed. The in-run pass defers
# such an injection while no retirement has yet been seen after it, because the answer is not knowable yet, which is
# the same shape the data half uses while its revealing retirement has not arrived.
# WHY NOT A TIME WINDOW KEYED ON THE FINISH REQUEST, which was the first idea: the finish request was seen at cycle
# 21433 and the core kept retiring for another 45 cycles, so a finish-keyed rule would have excused injections that
# were genuinely consumed and checkable. The retirement test is strictly narrower.

